  "findings": [
    "Native completion uses a Runtime-owned fixed IRQ mailbox; BO task mutex is forbidden in IRQ. Worker publishes fences and releases backing.",
    "First boot exceeded the 64-KB graphics worker stack because array-value loops copied entire 17-KB job tables. Pool-address iteration removed the copies without enlarging the stack.",
    "Private Test image initially lacked SSHD. Canonical module-catalog now derives exactly Test plus SSHD for this fixture; no production profile change.",
    "DISPLAYD needed its explicit R4DESK import for input and hosted process launch; both are now part of the actual guest proof.",
    "Fresh private images regenerate their SSH host key. The runner resets only its own private known_hosts before the fresh run.",
    "Cross-timeline BO hazards require an explicit dependency path. Cancellable implicit predecessor waits are not inherited as resource order."
  ],
  "reproduce": "Restore the saved PS7/askpass helper files under Temp/gfx-07906 at this source revision, build Kernel, DisplayDiag, Example and SshService with owner starters, then run Run-Qemu.ps1 for native and software sequentially. SMP4, private fresh 2048-MB media, bounded watchdog, real QMP keyboard and localhost SSH. Test AUTOEXEC is restored byte-for-byte.",
  "limitations": [
    "The EXAMPLE fixture retains real BOs and acknowledges from a real timer IRQ but deliberately performs no GPU DMA. Copy requests fail rather than claim copied native pixels.",
    "Native shader commands, NVIDIA registers, GPU caches/PTEs and actual scanout/VBlank are future driver work.",
    "BO conflict checking is conservative per object; nonoverlapping ranges still need ordering.",
    "Builds and probes ran on Debian; shared Windows PowerShell flow was not executed."
  ]
}
